 "steps": [
  {
   "say": "Here's the TMC2209 module. The left row of pins takes control signals, and the right row takes power and the motor.",
   "scene": [
    {
     "do": "highlight",
     "target": "tmc"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "Run three wires: GPIO 18 to STEP, GPIO 19 to DIR, and GPIO 5 to EN. EN is active low, so the motor only runs when that pin is low.",
   "scene": [
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "ws"
    },
    {
     "delay": 0.4,
     "do": "show",
     "target": "wd"
    },
    {
     "delay": 0.8,
     "do": "show",
     "target": "we"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "Logic power is the ESP32's 3V3 pin to VIO, and GND to GND.",
   "scene": [
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "wv"
    },
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "wg"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "The motor gets its own 12 to 24 volt supply on VM and GND, with a 100 microfarad capacitor across it. Make sure that ground is shared with the ESP32.",
   "scene": [
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "wm"
    },
    {
     "do": "highlight",
     "target": "cap"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "say": "Finally, the NEMA 17's four wires go to A1, A2, B1 and B2, one coil per pair. Each pulse on STEP moves it one step, and DIR sets the direction.",
   "scene": [
    {
     "do": "show",
     "target": "coil"
    },
    {
     "along": "ws",
     "color": "#58a6ff",
     "do": "flow"
    },
    {
     "axis": "y",
     "do": "spin",
     "target": "nshaft",
     "value": 0.5
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
 "title": "ESP32 → TMC2209 → NEMA 17"
